      "provenance": { "pdSource": "Piano Sonata No. 14 in C-sharp minor Op. 27 No. 2 ('Moonlight'), first movement (Ludwig van Beethoven), published 1802 (Giovanni Cappi, Vienna); the rising 5-R-3rd triplet arpeggio ostinato, chord-relative, durations overlapped for the pedal-sustain feel. The third is the generic role '3' (resolves to the chord's own third), NOT the forced 'b3' token: Beethoven re-voices this figure to every chord, so it must come out minor on the i and MAJOR on the bVI and the dominant -- a hard-coded b3 would grind a minor third against every major chord in the loop" },
